 "intro": "Near Lauron in eastern Spain, 76 BC. Quintus Sertorius, a Roman rebel, rules much of Spain and is besieging Lauron. You are the young Gnaeus Pompeius, later called Pompey the Great, sent by the Senate.",
 "debrief": "In Plutarch’s and Frontinus’s accounts, Pompey thought he had Sertorius trapped, but Sertorius had hidden a force behind Pompey’s own camp. He then ambushed Pompey’s foragers, and the legion sent to rescue them; nearly 10,000 men were lost. Pompey, threatened from behind, had to watch Sertorius take and burn Lauron. Sertorius is said to have remarked that Sulla’s pupil should have looked behind him. The other choices are what-ifs.",
